- src/main/java/net/sf/jabref/gui/help/HelpAction.java: Add a set of available help language codes and update openHelpPage() to use the chosen language only if a corresponding help page exists; otherwise fall back to English. Also added a short comment reminding to register new help languages in the set. Uses StringBuilder to construct the URL.", "id": 44497345}}

{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 100, "additional_feedback": "", "h": [], "hi": [], "textWords": 115, "aiWords": 0, "fakePercentage": 0.0, "specialIndexes": [], "specialSentences": [], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/18/2ee03251-f4a7-4b74-a4dc-9bfb7ca1ad49", "feedback": "Your Text is Human Written", "input_text": "Fixes #7986

This PR fixes the Optional Fields column visibility issue in the entry editor when the available width is small. In the compressed two-column layout the first column could disappear; to fix this both expandable columns are now given equal weight by setting columnExpand.setPercentWidth(40) in FieldsEditorTab so they grow/shrink equally.

The PR also refactors OptionalFieldsTab and OptionalFields2Tab into a new OptionalFieldsTabBase to remove duplicated code. The base class centralizes the tab setup (title, tooltip, icon) and the logic to determine which optional fields to show (primary vs. secondary) using a boolean flag and BibEntryTypesManager. The existing tabs now delegate to this new base class. Minor import cleanup was performed as part of the change.", "id": 44492202}}

