{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 50, "additional_feedback": "", "h": ["This pull request addresses threading issues in the `AbbreviateAction` class by ensuring that UI updates are executed on the JavaFX thread.", "Previously, these updates were being performed in background threads, which led to exceptions such as `IllegalStateException` and `IndexOutOfBoundsException`.", "The changes involve wrapping the `undoableAbbreviator.abbreviate` method calls in `UiTaskExecutor.runInJavaFXThread`, ensuring that they are executed on the correct thread.", "The issue is fixed as referenced from [this StackOverflow answer](https://stackoverflow.com/a/40640583).", "Manual testing confirmed that no exceptions occur after the fix."], "hi": [], "textWords": 80, "aiWords": 78, "fakePercentage": 97.5, "specialIndexes": [], "specialSentences": [], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/18/79ec233d-45d1-425c-972d-736b03bd2c56", "feedback": "Your Text contains mixed signals, with some parts generated by AI/GPT", "input_text": "This pull request addresses threading issues in the `AbbreviateAction` class by ensuring that UI updates are executed on the JavaFX thread. Previously, these updates were being performed in background threads, which led to exceptions such as `IllegalStateException` and `IndexOutOfBoundsException`. The changes involve wrapping the `undoableAbbreviator.abbreviate` method calls in `UiTaskExecutor.runInJavaFXThread`, ensuring that they are executed on the correct thread.

The issue is fixed as referenced from [this StackOverflow answer](https://stackoverflow.com/a/40640583). Manual testing confirmed that no exceptions occur after the fix.

Closes #12634", "id": 44497051}}

{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 100, "additional_feedback": "", "h": [], "hi": [], "textWords": 113, "aiWords": 0, "fakePercentage": 0.0, "specialIndexes": [1], "specialSentences": ["Changes:"], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/18/b3b12a37-3509-41f5-aca4-227c8496df6a", "feedback": "Your Text is Human Written", "input_text": "This PR fixes UI behavior when an invalid BibTeX key is entered and updates the changelog. Changes:

- Fix: EntryEditor no longer always pops up an error dialog when an invalid BibTeX key is detected. The code now sets the field to an invalid background and returns immediately; the JOptionPane is only shown when the current thread is not the Swing Event Dispatch Thread (and requestFocus() is invoked in that case). This prevents the previous problematic dialog behavior that could lead to crashes or UI issues when handling invalid keys.

- Docs: CHANGELOG.md updated — link formatting corrected for existing fixes and a new entry added for #1882 ("Crash after saving illegal bibtexkey in entry editor").", "id": 44494403}}

{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 100, "additional_feedback": "", "h": [], "hi": [], "textWords": 78, "aiWords": 0, "fakePercentage": 0.0, "specialIndexes": [], "specialSentences": [], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/18/23581e0b-2d0a-460e-b346-96af5f918ba1", "feedback": "Your Text is Human Written", "input_text": "Only show the recovery dialog when a .sav file has actual changes.

Previously, after a forced shutdown JabRef could display a recovery dialog even if the .sav file had not changed, causing unnecessary nagging on restart. This change ensures we verify whether the .sav file contains meaningful modifications before presenting the recovery dialog; if there are no changes, no dialog is shown.

This addresses the immediate symptom reported in #6109. The larger underlying issue will be investigated separately.", "id": 44497048}}

{"success": true, "code": 200, "message": "Detection complete", "data": {"sentences": [], "isHuman": 100, "additional_feedback": "", "h": [], "hi": [], "textWords": 87, "aiWords": 0, "fakePercentage": 0.0, "specialIndexes": [], "specialSentences": [], "originalParagraph": "2026/2/18/aad42c48-bd3f-4d3e-94a6-1826d2a805b9", "feedback": "Your Text is Human Written", "input_text": "Initialize PreviewPanel earlier to prevent NPE on delete

Moved preview initialization to occur before setupMainPanel() so the preview and its JavaFX container are available when other components (such as deletion handlers and the global search highlight listener) are set up. This change: creates the PreviewPanel, registers it with the global search bar on the JavaFX thread, and wraps it with CustomJFXPanel up front. The duplicate later initialization was removed. Additionally tightened parentheses in the EntryRemovedListener conditional (no behavior change).

Fixes #3584 — follow-up to #3574. Manually tested.", "id": 44497211}}

